The condition is $|\{v \mid d(v) \text{ is even}\}| = |\{v \mid d(v) \text{ is odd}\}|$.
Since there are $N$ vertices in total, and vertex 1 is at distance 0 (even), the number of vertices at even distance is at least 1.
Let $E$ be the set of vertices with even distance, and $O$ be the set of vertices with odd distance.
We require $|E| = |O|$. Since $|E| + |O| = N$ and $N$ is even, this implies $|E| = |O| = N/2$.
